Summary
I've successfully implemented weighted probability for random item finding based on item rarity. Here's what was implemented:
Changes Made in CombatCoordinator.cs:
1.	Modified AwardRandomItemsAfterCombat method:
•	Changed line 311 from allItems[_random.Next(allItems.Count)] to SelectItemByRarityWeight(allItems)
•	Now uses weighted selection instead of uniform random selection
2.	Added new SelectItemByRarityWeight method:
•	Uses the rarity weights you specified:
•	Common: 58% probability
•	Uncommon: 25% probability
•	Rare: 10% probability
•	VeryRare: 4% probability
•	Legendary: 2% probability
•	Unique: 1% probability
•	Implements weighted random selection algorithm:
1.	Calculates total weight by summing all item weights
2.	Generates a random number between 0 and total weight
3.	Iterates through items cumulatively until reaching the random value
4.	Returns the selected item
How It Works:
When random items are found after combat:
1.	The system determines how many items to find using the existing dice roll mechanism
2.	For each item to be found, SelectItemByRarityWeight is called
3.	The method assigns each item a weight based on its rarity
4.	Common items have the highest weight (58), making them most likely to be selected
5.	Unique items have the lowest weight (1), making them extremely rare
6.	Items with undefined rarity default to Common weight
Example:
If there are 100 items with the following rarities:
•	60 Common items (60 × 58 = 3,480 total weight)
•	30 Uncommon items (30 × 25 = 750 total weight)
•	10 Rare items (10 × 10 = 100 total weight)
The probability of selecting:
•	A Common item: ~82.5%
•	An Uncommon item: ~14.2%
•	A Rare item: ~3.3%
This creates a natural progression where common items are found frequently, while legendary and unique items are truly special discoveries!
